19. AUM Analysis

Assets Under Management (AUM) is an important measure of fund size.

The project created a dedicated:

fact_aum

table containing:

AMFI code
AUM in crore
Expense ratio
Morningstar rating

AUM can be analyzed across fund houses, categories, and individual schemes to understand which funds attract larger asset bases.

20. Expense Ratio Analysis

Expense ratio represents the operating expenses charged by a mutual fund relative to its assets.

The project validates expense ratio values and includes the metric in the analytical database.

Expense ratio can be compared with:

Returns
Sharpe ratio
Fund category
Fund size
Risk grade

This helps evaluate whether higher costs are associated with stronger performance.

21. Mutual Fund Recommendation Analysis

The project also includes a recommendation component.

Fund selection can consider multiple metrics rather than relying only on returns.

Potential criteria include:

Higher long-term returns
Positive alpha
Higher Sharpe ratio
Higher Sortino ratio
Lower volatility
Lower maximum drawdown
Reasonable expense ratio
Morningstar rating
Risk grade

This creates a more balanced approach to fund evaluation.

The recommendation analysis is intended as an analytical aid and should not be considered personalized financial advice.

